{"boundary": "post_model_pre_tool", "tool_calls": [{"args": {"content": "# Fix for Sphinx Python Domain :type: and :rtype: Cross-Reference Issue\n\n## Problem Description\n\nWhen using `:type:` or `:rtype:` fields in Python docstrings within Sphinx documentation, false \"more than one target found\" warnings were generated when the same class name existed in both a parent module and its submodules.\n\n### Example Scenario\n\nGiven the following structure:\n- `mod.A` (class in parent module)\n- `mod.submod.A` (class in submodule)\n\nWhen documenting a function in module `mod`:\n```python\n.. py:currentmodule:: mod\n\n.. py:function:: func(a)\n\n   :param A a: Parameter of type A\n   :type a: A\n   :rtype: A\n```\n\n**Before Fix**: Sphinx would warn about ambiguity, finding both `mod.A` and `mod.submod.A` as potential matches.\n\n**After Fix**: Sphinx correctly resolves to `mod.A` (the class in the current module) without warnings.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `/testbed/sphinx/domains/python.py`, the `find_obj()` method's fuzzy search mode (searchmode=1) was returning ALL objects ending with the target name (`.name`), without considering the module context hierarchy.\n\nThe fuzzy search at lines 1269-1273 would find all matches like:\n- `mod.A`\n- `mod.submod.A`  \n- `mod.submod.deeper.A`\n\nAnd return them all, causing Sphinx to issue ambiguity warnings even when one match was clearly more appropriate given the current module context.\n\n## Solution\n\nModified the fuzzy search logic in `find_obj()` (lines 1274-1286) to implement a module-aware prioritization strategy:\n\n1. **First**: Look for exact matches in the current module (`modname.name`)\n2. **Second**: If no exact match, look for matches in submodules (`modname.*`)\n3. **Third**: If no module context match exists, return all matches (preserving original behavior for legitimate ambiguity cases)\n\n### Code Changes\n\nFile: `/testbed/sphinx/domains/python.py`\nLocation: Lines 1274-1286 (within the `find_obj()` method)\n\n```python\n# if there are multiple matches, prefer matches in the current module\nif len(matches) > 1 and modname:\n    # first try to find an exact match in the current module\n    exact_match = [(oname, obj) for oname, obj in matches\n                 if oname == modname + searchname]\n    if exact_match:\n        matches = exact_match\n    else:\n        # if no exact match, look for matches in submodules\n        module_matches = [(oname, obj) for oname, obj in matches\n                        if oname.startswith(modname + '.')]\n        if module_matches:\n            matches = module_matches\n```\n\n## Test Cases\n\nThe fix correctly handles the following scenarios:\n\n### Test 1: Exact match in current module\n- **Context**: `modname='mod'`, looking for `A`\n- **Objects**: `mod.A`, `mod.submod.A`, `mod.submod.deeper.A`\n- **Result**: Resolves to `mod.A` (exact match)\n- **Status**: ✓ PASS\n\n### Test 2: Exact match in submodule\n- **Context**: `modname='mod.submod'`, looking for `A`\n- **Objects**: `mod.A`, `mod.submod.A`, `mod.submod.deeper.A`\n- **Result**: Resolves to `mod.submod.A` (exact match)\n- **Status**: ✓ PASS\n\n### Test 3: No module context match\n- **Context**: `modname='other'`, looking for `A`\n- **Objects**: `mod.A`, `mod.submod.A`, `mod.submod.deeper.A`\n- **Result**: Returns all matches (legitimate ambiguity)\n- **Status**: ✓ PASS\n\n### Test 4: Only submodule match exists\n- **Context**: `modname='mod'`, looking for `A`\n- **Objects**: `mod.submod.A`, `other.A`\n- **Result**: Resolves to `mod.submod.A` (fallback to submodule)\n- **Status**: ✓ PASS\n\n## Impact\n\nThis fix:\n- ✅ Eliminates false positive ambiguity warnings\n- ✅ Improves user experience when documenting hierarchical module structures\n- ✅ Preserves existing behavior for legitimate ambiguity cases\n- ✅ Follows Python's natural name resolution semantics (prefer local scope)\n- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality\n\n## Files Modified\n\n- `/testbed/sphinx/domains/python.py` (lines 1274-1286)\n\n## Verification\n\nThe fix logic has been tested with multiple scenarios and confirmed to work correctly.\nSee `/tmp/test_improved_logic.py` for detailed test cases.\n", "path": "/testbed/FIX_SUMMARY.md"}, "id": "toolu_hyTKbtiPjqiigVxc1rh1WR", "name": "file_write"}], "tool_results": [], "task_turn": 48, "text": "<summary>Creating a file to document the fix for future reference and creating a summary report</summary>", "synopsis": "Creating a file to document the fix for future reference and creating a summary report", "archive_sequence": 95, "archived_at": 1790186540.6715312}
